        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This looks like conflicting with [default scrolling mappings](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/68d4478920c7afdfa21c13706464e275d9ce3255/doc/mini-completion.txt#L294-L298) of 'mini.completion'. There are two approaches to resolve this:\r\n\r\n- Create your own mappings *after* calling `require('mini.completion').setup()`.\r\n- Instruct 'mini.completion' to not create scrolling mappings (or use different keys for it). The \"not create at all\" approach is something like this:\r\n\r\n    ```lua\r\n    require('mini.completion').setup({\r\n      mappings = { scroll_down = '', scroll_up = '' }\r\n    })\r\n    ```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This looks like conflicting with <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/68d4478920c7afdfa21c13706464e275d9ce3255/doc/mini-completion.txt#L294-L298\">default scrolling mappings</a> of 'mini.completion'. There are two approaches to resolve this:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Create your own mappings <em>after</em> calling <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.completion').setup()</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Instruct 'mini.completion' to not create scrolling mappings (or use different keys for it). The \"not create at all\" approach is something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.completion').setup({\n  mappings = { scroll_down = '', scroll_up = '' }\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.completion<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">scroll_down</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">scroll_up</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}\n})</pre></div>\n</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "This looks like conflicting with default scrolling mappings of 'mini.completion'. There are two approaches to resolve this:\n\n\nCreate your own mappings after calling require('mini.completion').setup().\n\n\nInstruct 'mini.completion' to not create scrolling mappings (or use different keys for it). The \"not create at all\" approach is something like this:\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({\n  mappings = { scroll_down = '', scroll_up = '' }\n})",
