                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Yes, that's exactly the issue I'm encountering, though I should have made it clearer:\r\n\r\nThe default configuration of `mini.completion` causes my key bindings for <kbd>C-f</kbd> and <kbd>C-b</kbd> to become unworkable. \r\n\r\nHowever, what I want to achieve is: when the popup of `mini.completion` appears, `C-f` and `C-b` should scroll the popup; when there is no popup, `C-f` and `C-b` fallback to my previous key bindings (just like `blink.cmp` does, I'm using it now and I'd like to migrate to `mini.completion`). \r\n\r\nIs this kind of requirement achievable?",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, that's exactly the issue I'm encountering, though I should have made it clearer:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The default configuration of <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> causes my key bindings for <kbd>C-f</kbd> and <kbd>C-b</kbd> to become unworkable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, what I want to achieve is: when the popup of <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> appears, <code class=\"notranslate\">C-f</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">C-b</code> should scroll the popup; when there is no popup, <code class=\"notranslate\">C-f</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">C-b</code> fallback to my previous key bindings (just like <code class=\"notranslate\">blink.cmp</code> does, I'm using it now and I'd like to migrate to <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is this kind of requirement achievable?</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, that's exactly the issue I'm encountering, though I should have made it clearer:\nThe default configuration of mini.completion causes my key bindings for C-f and C-b to become unworkable.\nHowever, what I want to achieve is: when the popup of mini.completion appears, C-f and C-b should scroll the popup; when there is no popup, C-f and C-b fallback to my previous key bindings (just like blink.cmp does, I'm using it now and I'd like to migrate to mini.completion).\nIs this kind of requirement achievable?",
