                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, this is also possible with the help of [`MiniCompletion.scroll()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-completion.html#minicompletion.scroll). Like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.completion').setup()\r\n\r\nlocal scroll_down_or_right = function() return MiniCompletion.scroll('down') and '' or '<Right>' end\r\nlocal scroll_up_or_left = function() return MiniCompletion.scroll('up') and '' or '<Left>' end\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-f>', scroll_down_or_right, { expr = true })\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-b>', scroll_up_or_left, { expr = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `return a and b or c` is a Lua idiom for the (imitation of) ternary operator. Here it means \"if scroll is scheduled, do nothing else, otherwise act like an arrow key\" (the `expr = true` in mappings is important).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, this is also possible with the help of <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-completion.html#minicompletion.scroll\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniCompletion.scroll()</code></a>. Like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.completion').setup()\n\nlocal scroll_down_or_right = function() return MiniCompletion.scroll('down') and '' or '&lt;Right&gt;' end\nlocal scroll_up_or_left = function() return MiniCompletion.scroll('up') and '' or '&lt;Left&gt;' end\n\nvim.keymap.set('i', '&lt;C-f&gt;', scroll_down_or_right, { expr = true })\nvim.keymap.set('i', '&lt;C-b&gt;', scroll_up_or_left, { expr = true })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.completion<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">scroll_down_or_right</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniCompletion</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">scroll</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>down<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Right&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">scroll_up_or_left</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniCompletion</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">scroll</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>up<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Left&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-f&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">scroll_down_or_right</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">expr</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> })\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-b&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">scroll_up_or_left</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">expr</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">return a and b or c</code> is a Lua idiom for the (imitation of) ternary operator. Here it means \"if scroll is scheduled, do nothing else, otherwise act like an arrow key\" (the <code class=\"notranslate\">expr = true</code> in mappings is important).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, this is also possible with the help of MiniCompletion.scroll(). Like this:\nrequire('mini.completion').setup()\n\nlocal scroll_down_or_right = function() return MiniCompletion.scroll('down') and '' or '<Right>' end\nlocal scroll_up_or_left = function() return MiniCompletion.scroll('up') and '' or '<Left>' end\n\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-f>', scroll_down_or_right, { expr = true })\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-b>', scroll_up_or_left, { expr = true })\nThe return a and b or c is a Lua idiom for the (imitation of) ternary operator. Here it means \"if scroll is scheduled, do nothing else, otherwise act like an arrow key\" (the expr = true in mappings is important).",
